      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1931 Mose Coleman noticed his onions were sweeter, launching the Vidalia onion that would later be named Georgia’s official vegetable in 1990.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vidalia%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Altama Museum of Art & History, housed in the 1911 Brazell House, displays 18th‑century American and European prints and porcelain.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
